## 9. REAL-TIME EMAIL SYNCHRONIZATION ENGINE

Implement a reliable server-side synchronization service.

The system must:

- Fetch new messages from connected providers.
- Persist imported messages.
- Update existing threads.
- Track provider message identifiers.
- Store synchronization checkpoints.
- Prevent duplicate imports.
- Retry temporary provider errors.
- Respect rate limits.
- Recover after process restarts.
- Detect expired tokens.
- Report synchronization delays.
- Preserve local staff notes and assignments.

Use provider push notifications or webhooks where supported and operationally configured.

Provide a polling fallback for providers without push support.

